==Trivia==
*In Greek Mythology, [[wikipedia:Cerberus|Cerberus]] is the canine guardian of the underworld who has three heads like how these netdwellers are a group of three.
**Cerberus Kids' Japanese name, Keruberōzu (ケルベローズ), can be taken as "Cerbellows" or "Cerberrows" and is a pun on ケルベロス ''Keruberosu'' (Cerberus) and フェローズ ''ferōzu'' (fellows).
*According to their Japanese description, these stickmen have actual names. From left to right, they are Tiablo (ティアブロ ''Tiaburo''), Baal (バール ''Bāru'') and Mephisto (メフィスト ''Mefisuto'').
**Tiablo is one letter away from ''diablo'', the Spanish word for devil.
**Baal is another name for the Christian demon [[wikipedia:Bael (demon)|Bael]].
**Mephisto takes his name from [[wikipedia:Mephistopheles|Mephistopheles]], a Faustian demon.
**They share their names with the three [[wikia:diablo:Prime Evil|Prime Evils]] from the ''[[wikipedia:Diablo (series)|Diablo]]'' franchise – with the exception of Tiablo, which is off by one letter.
*Their design is somewhat similar to The Three Robbers from the [https://www.amazon.com/Three-Robbers-Tomi-Ungerer/dp/0714848778 picture book] and [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ijn80UFqDgQ animation] of the same name, though with pointier hats and no other clothing. "Used to be low-level [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies" could refer to how the robbers' adopted children wear red versions of their foster parents' outfits.
*Cerberus Kids and [[Sir Seal]] have opposite Japanese descriptions. Cerberus Kids were Red until they came to Tokyo, while Sir Seal dyed himself Red after coming to Tokyo.
*They have the lowest health and money drop of all [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku Enemies]].
*They were technically an event enemy for a short time, as they were initially exclusive to the [[Empress' Research]] stages and [[Wrath of Hell (Deadly)|The Great Diablo]].

